{
  "id": "COMPOUND:41815 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Cabraleone is implicated in the target pathway leading to Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple intermediates, all of which are involved in the modulation of phosphodiesterase activity. The evidence suggests that Cabraleone acts as a target for compounds that are themselves involved in the regulation of phosphodiesterase 6C, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving the inhibition of this enzyme. The shared involvement of BALL-1 and Luteolin-7-O-Glucuronic Acid in the target pathway highlights a possible role in the metabolic or signaling pathways that influence phosphodiesterase 6C activity. The consistent presence of these intermediates across different pathways supports the notion that Cabraleone is linked to Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of molecular interactions that are likely relevant to its pharmacological effects. The integration of these findings suggests a broader role for Cabraleone in modulating phosphodiesterase 6C, potentially through the regulation of downstream targets that influence enzyme activity.",
